<title>SWEDEN: ABB shares slide after 1996 result.</title>
<headline>ABB shares slide after 1996 result.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish listed shares in international engineer ABB slid on the Stockholm bourse on Thursday after the company posted a worse-than-expected report for 1996.</p>
<p>At 1105 GMT ABB AB shares were 51 crowns lower at 854 crowns.</p>
<p>The company posted a group net profit of $1.23 billion against market expectations of a profit of $1.30 billion. The company also proposed to split ABB AB shares in a 10-for-one split.</p>
<p>&quot;People are a bit disappointed about the result,&quot; said one broker.</p>
<p>&quot;A split always usually has a positive effect but this time it is overshadowed by the profit that was worse than expected.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
